{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-02T17:01:06.282Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\n**Implemented** (`src/core/foundation/`):\n- **`harness-containment.ts`** (new): `HarnessContainment` type, one named reporter per harness with the exact delta messages, the `HARNESS_CONTAINMENT` record keyed by `HarnessName`, and `attachContainment` for the catalog.\n- **`harness-catalog.ts`**: `containment` is now required and typed `(config) => HarnessContainment`; the catalog attaches each reporter as it builds `HARNESS_CATALOG` (file stays at 245 lines).\n- **`config-claude.ts`**: `diagnoseClaude` returns only its `harness-version` check; `claudeContainment` keeps its current text.\n- **`doctor.ts`**: adds one `harness-containment` check after `harness` + `diagnose` checks, only when `config` passed, whether or not the probe passed, carrying `warning: true`, without naming any harness.\n\n**Tests**:\n- New `tests/harness-containment.test.ts` drives `runDoctorChecks` via the `loadConfig`/`probeValidator` seams for every harness (all messages, agy failure, both warnings, Pi ordering).\n- Updated `tests/doctor.test.ts`, `tests/codex/adapter.test.ts`, `tests/pi/doctor.test.ts` for the new check name/counts.\n\n**Verification**:\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/harness-containment.test.ts` → 9 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify` → exit 0.\n\nOne disclosed tension in the result (`## Deviated` / `## Missing context`): `tests/claude/exec-config.test.ts` (not in scope) strictly asserts the catalog's Claude containment equals a string, so Claude's reporter reuses `claudeContainment` and doctor normalizes the string. The result file is at `openspec/changes/137-safer-harness-defaults/.run/results/2.md`."}}
